messages:
maria: Running into a weird one — our sample app works in Node but fails on Deno deploy with a crypto/fetch error. stack: `TypeError: globalThis.crypto is undefined` and later `TypeError: fetch is not a function`

maria: We're using the JS SDK from npm via Skypack import in deno: `import Inference from 'https://cdn.skypack.dev/@redwood-inference/js-sdk'` — any recommended pattern for Deno/Bun?

devin: yeah Deno doesn't expose the same globals as Node. Quick answers: set up an import_map + polyfill crypto, or use a Deno-specific build (if we publish one). Did you try `globalThis.crypto = (await import('https://deno.land/std@0.203.0/crypto/mod.ts')).webcrypto`?

kevin: also watch typings — TS complains about DOM lib missing for `CryptoKey` etc. add "lib": ["esnext","dom"] to tsconfig or use `--lib=dom` with deno types.

sam: for Bun, fetch exists but headers handling differs (immutable Headers weirdness). We ran into subtle `body used` errors. It's a mix of runtime APIs. Usually a tiny runtime guard in the SDK helps.

maria: example deno.json that helped me: 
```json
{
  "importMap": "./import_map.json",
  "tasks": {},
  "unstable": true
}
```

maria: and import_map.json to point at the ESM entry we tested: 
```json
{
  "imports": {
    "@redwood-inference/": "./esm/"
  }
}
```

devin: one more pattern: runtime feature detection in app before importing SDK internals: 
```js
if (!globalThis.crypto) {
  const { webcrypto } = await import('https://deno.land/std@0.203.0/crypto/mod.ts');
  globalThis.crypto = webcrypto;
}
if (!globalThis.fetch) {
  // tiny fetch polyfill or use undici for Node-like behavior
}
```

kevin: for typing pain in Deno you can also add a small ambient file `globals.d.ts` with `declare var fetch: typeof globalThis.fetch;` — but better is publishing a `deno.d.ts` that re-exports types from `dom` so consumers don't have to tweak tsconfig.

edge-bot: heads-up: CI flake seen on last couple of runs when running SDK tests under Bun — failing test: `should retry 429` due to different network timing. Filing an issue? :warning:

sam: Filing one is good. In the meantime, guard retry behavior by making timeout/retry configurable via `createClient({ retry: { maxAttempts: 3, backoffMs: 200 } })` so runtime-specific network quirks don't break default tests.

maria: thanks — I'll try the import_map + crypto shim route. If it still fails I'll paste a minimal repro. Also curious if we should add a `dist/deno` build in the SDK to avoid CDN shenanigans.

devin: +1 on dist/deno. We can publish a lightweight ESM bundle that only uses Web APIs and documents required globals. Makes onboarding smoother for Deno/Bun users.

maria: great, will ping again with repro. :slightly_smiling_face:
